HST Office: app-wide dialogs (Find and Replace, Hyperlink, Options, Special Characters, Spelling, PDF Options,
Thesaurus, Templates, Paste Special, Document Properties, Alt Text, Extension Manager, Digital Signatures,
Compress Image, Customize, About, Macro Selector) follow the dialog layout rulebook.

- Margins: dialogs without tabs have a 12 px border; tabbed dialogs keep 6 px on the shell and every tab page
  (and every Options page) has a 12 px border, so pages do not touch the tab column and tabs do not jump.
- Find and Replace: the command buttons, the options expander and the Go To panel line up with the search
  fields (12 px inside); the gap above the command row and the options is the 12 px group gap.
- Special Characters: both tab pages get the 12 px page border; the search, font and block labels sit 4 px
  above their fields.
- Customize: the target list and its gear menu are 6 px apart; the keyboard page's lists ask for 8 and 7 rows
  instead of 10 and 9 so the dialog fits a 1366x768 screen (the keyboard page is its tallest).
- Options: on small screens the page area is clamped to 70 % of the screen height (was 80 %), so the dialog with
  its frame fits a 1366x768 work area; larger screens keep the 30-row page area.
- Templates: 12 px between the body and the button row; the two view toggles are 6 px apart.
- Find and Replace: the search status line, which wraps, shows its whole text (no ellipsis).
- Document Properties: the field labels of the General, Description, Statistics pages, PDF signing and Compress
  Image start-align with their column; the Description page keeps one 12 px inset (its viewport's).
No widget id, handler, tab order, access key, string or accessible name changes.
Checked by tests/unit/test_ui_layout_rulebook.py and tests/runtime/hst_dialog_layout_check.py
(cases of this group: tests/runtime/data/dialog-layout-d.json).

